## Database configuration

### 1. Create the database

The whole schema (DDL) and the test data (DML, 30+ rows in the main tables) are in `docs/database.sql`. The script creates the `erp_little_horizons` database from scratch.

```bash
mysql -u root -p --default-character-set=utf8mb4 < docs/database.sql
```

With Docker:

```bash
docker exec -i mysql_container mysql -uroot -p<password> --default-character-set=utf8mb4 < docs/database.sql
```

### 2. Configure credentials

Copy `config.example.txt` to `config.txt` in the project root (next to `pom.xml`) and edit the three keys:

```
db.url=jdbc:mysql://localhost:3307/erp_little_horizons?useUnicode=true&characterEncoding=utf8&serverTimezone=America/Bogota
db.user=root
db.password=your_password_here
```

`config.txt` is listed in `.gitignore` so the password is never committed.

### 3. Install the JDBC driver

Nothing to install by hand: Maven downloads `mysql-connector-j` from the dependency declared in `pom.xml`. In IntelliJ, use *Maven > Reload All Maven Projects* if the driver is not found.

